# Allow-list build context: ignore everything, then re-include only what the
# image needs. Secrets (.env*), docs, SDK tooling, tests, run artefacts and
# VCS metadata can therefore never enter the build context.
*

!manage.py
!VERSION
!config/
!webinars/
!docker/
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!LICENSE
# Public guides served as MCP resources (webinars/mcp_resources.GUIDES).
!README.md
!docs/implementation-guide.md
!docs/operations.md
!docs/integration.md
!docs/mcp.md
!docs/management-api.md
!docs/api-reference.md
!docs/webhooks.md
!docs/field-dictionary.md
!docs/field-mapping.md
!docs/waiting-room.md
!docs/studio.md
!docs/email.md
!docs/browser-integration.md
!docs/native-integrations.md
!docs/security.md
!docs/tickets.md
!docs/hosting.md
!docs/kits.md

# Re-exclude junk inside allowed directories.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/*.sqlite3
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Explicitly listed for reviewers (already excluded by "*" above):
# sdk/ tests/ .runs/ examples/ .git/ .env .env.* compose.yaml, and every docs/*.md and
# *.md not re-included above.
